{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"The repaired utility accepts an output pathname and successfully exports the complete invoices.csv contents.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed script accepts one destination argument. Multiple executions, including as an ordinary user and after restart, produced output identical to the three-line source.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4a553cfe634e4ddf","cmd-e6e4d78a3a394656","cmd-8d04cdfecc9b4fcf","cmd-3a69f0a309a648f3"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Concurrent exports use distinct private temporary files and complete without corrupting the export.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Six simultaneous ordinary-user exports exposed six unique mode-0600 temporary files owned by that user. All processes succeeded, the final destination matched the source, and no temporary files remained.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8b32ca340bdf4e9f"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"A pre-existing symlink cannot redirect export writes into the protected sentinel.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The seeded symlink targeting protected.txt remained present during a successful export without changing the sentinel. The attack symlink was recreated after restart with the same safe result. The implementation uses a unique destination-adjacent temporary file and rename rather than the vulnerable fixed path.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a594823f81064944","cmd-4a553cfe634e4ddf","cmd-e6e4d78a3a394656","cmd-3a69f0a309a648f3"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Export failures leave the prior destination intact, and temporary files are removed when the utility exits.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A forced rename failure returned nonzero while preserving the destination checksum and contents and leaving no temporary residue. Success, concurrent execution, and post-restart checks also showed zero residue; the installed exit trap supports cleanup across ordinary failure paths.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4a553cfe634e4ddf","cmd-e6e4d78a3a394656","cmd-8b32ca340bdf4e9f","cmd-0f53cf98f5554069","cmd-3a69f0a309a648f3"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"The source invoice data and protected sentinel are preserved.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Final source and sentinel hashes exactly match their prepared baseline values, including after attack testing and restart.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-16be77f5162640d5","cmd-3a69f0a309a648f3"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Retain the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"RHEL 10.0 and kernel 6.12.0-55.9.1.el10_0 remained unchanged. The shell utility was syntax-checked and successfully exercised using the platform's installed shell and core utilities before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-fe72994cd2b74e48","cmd-4a553cfe634e4ddf","cmd-8d04cdfecc9b4fcf","cmd-3a69f0a309a648f3","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. The persistent utility replacement was required; deletion of the seeded malicious symlink was appropriate cleanup and preserved its target. All test directories, outputs, shims, and recreated attack artifacts were bounded and removed. The first concurrency probe had faulty test-directory permissions but was fully cleaned and directly informed the corrected bounded probe, so it is not assessed as an unrelated experiment. The mandated restart was acknowledged and fully evidenced. Final snapshots show no failed services, damaged package state, unexpected listeners, or executor test residue; temporary-file differences are normal systemd-private directories from the new boot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-4a553cfe634e4ddf","cmd-53770a8e8d1142a2","cmd-16be77f5162640d5","cmd-3ec980b6820640f1","cmd-3a69f0a309a648f3","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied. The exporter uses unique private temporary files and atomic replacement, preserves complete invoice data and the sentinel under concurrency and the seeded symlink attack, preserves an existing destination on failure, and cleans temporary artifacts. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart baseline, acknowledged restart, changed boot identity corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered system, SSH, data, and export behavior.","limitations":["Signal and every possible early-exit path were not dynamically injected; cleanup on those paths is supported primarily by inspection of the installed traps, alongside direct success and rename-failure tests.","No independent lifecycle snapshot inventories the task directory itself; final task state is established by executor commands, while lifecycle evidence independently confirms platform, boot, service, listener, temporary-file, and package health."]}
